# Committed on purpose: NEXT_PUBLIC_* values are compiled into the client
# bundle and are public by definition. Never add a secret to this file —
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY, RESEND_API_KEY and IP_HASH_SALT live only in
# Vercel's encrypted environment variables. CI greps for secret-shaped
# strings and fails the build if one is committed.
#
# DOMAIN CUTOVER — do these in order, then change the line below:
#   1. Buy the domain and add it to the Vercel project (Settings → Domains)
#   2. Wait for the certificate to issue and confirm the domain loads
#   3. Verify the same domain in Resend and set EMAIL_FROM
#   4. Only then point this at the new domain and redeploy
#
# Pointing this at a hostname that doesn't serve this build is what caused
# the canonical-tag incident recorded in docs/adr/0003 — the canonical tag
# told Google to index a stale deployment. Don't repeat it: this value must
# always be a hostname that is live and serving the current build.
#
# NOTE: this Vercel-generated alias changes if the Vercel project is renamed.
# If you rename the project, update this line to the new alias immediately.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://lumin-site-bay.vercel.app
